  "tutorialSkip": "Skip",
  "tutorialFinalOutro": "The bot is struck out and must now try for 10,000 itself. You now know all the rules: have a good game!",
  "tutorialFinalExact": "Three 4s: exactly 10,000! Taking it is automatic.",
  "tutorialFinalNoStop": "100: 9,600. In the final round, stopping isn't allowed: roll again.",
  "tutorialFinalIntro": "The bot has reached 10,000: this is the final round. To win, you must match it, which strikes it out. Stopping before that is forbidden.",
  "tutorialCollisionOutro": "The bot is struck out and falls back to 1,500. Reaching any of another player's lines, even an old one, strikes it out too.",
  "tutorialCollisionCollide": "Two aces: 200. You'd be at 2,000, the bot's score, in red on its radar. Stop to strike it out.",
  "tutorialCollisionIntro": "On the bot's line, the radar shows its scores you could strike out: reaching the same total pushes it back.",
  "tutorialInheritOutro": "After a bust, you always start again with 5 fresh dice. A hand that could no longer be banked is never offered.",
  "tutorialInheritStop": "An ace: the hand is worth 1,100. Stop.",
  "tutorialInheritTake": "The bot stopped at 1,000 leaving 2 dice. Take the hand: you start from its 1,000 points, and the 2 dice are rolled at once (you always roll at least once before stopping).",
  "tutorialInheritIntro": "When a player stops leaving dice, the next one may take them over, with their points as a base.",
  "tutorialExtensionOutro": "The extension lasts the whole turn, even for a 5 (100 instead of 50), and is cleared by hot dice.",
  "tutorialExtensionExtended": "A lone 2 is worth nothing… except here: after your three 2s, it's worth 100 (in red). The hand is 300: stop.",
  "tutorialExtensionBrelan": "Three 2s: 200. Reroll the last 2 dice.",
  "tutorialExtensionIntro": "After three of a kind, a lone die of the same value later in the turn is worth 100 points.",
  "tutorialBustOutro": "A bust marks the line with a dash; a second one strikes it out. At 0, a bust costs nothing.",
  "tutorialBustBarred": "Second bust: the 1,500 line is struck out, you fall back to 500, your previous score. Tap ✓.",
  "tutorialBustRollAgain": "Your line has a dash: a second bust would strike it out. Roll anyway.",
  "tutorialBustTiret": "Busted! The hand is lost, and your 1,500 line gets a dash. Tap ✓.",
  "tutorialBustIntro": "A roll that scores nothing is a bust: the current hand is lost. You have 1,500 points.",
  "tutorialHotDiceOutro": "Remember: never stop on a total ending in 50, and hot dice are always rerolled.",
  "tutorialHotDiceStop": "500: enough to enter, and no 50 at the end. Stop.",
  "tutorialHotDiceFives": "Two 5s, but they're optional: this selector chooses how many to keep. With both, 550 would end in 50: you couldn't stop. Choose 1.",
  "tutorialHotDiceFullHand": "Three 3s: 300, the hand rises to 450. Every die scored: hot dice! The button shows the total you would have; you reroll all 5 dice and can't stop.",
  "tutorialHotDiceKept": "The ace and the 5 are kept: the hand is worth 150. Reroll the other 3 dice.",
  "tutorialHotDiceIntro": "When every die scores, that's hot dice: you reroll all 5. And a lone 5 is sometimes optional.",
  "tutorialBasicsOutro": "700 points banked: you're in the game! From now on, each turn must score at least 200 points.",
  "tutorialBasicsBrelan": "Three 6s: three of a kind is worth 100 times its value, here 600 (three aces: 1000). The hand is worth 700, enough to enter: tap the hand to stop.",
  "tutorialBasicsAce": "Only the ace (100) and the 5 (50) score on their own: the ace is set aside. To enter the game you need 500 points in one turn: reroll the other 4 dice.",
  "tutorialBasicsIntro": "Welcome to Le 10000! The goal: reach exactly 10,000 points. On each turn, you roll 5 dice and set aside the ones that score.",
